6.4 Afferent Feedback System Specification

To facilitate embodiment, the copilot also drives a multi‑modal sensory feedback system. The design adheres to the following specifications:

· Tactile (ground contact / lift pressure): Pneumatic cuffs around the thighs and thorax. Pressure is proportional to ground reaction force (legs) and total lift (wings). Update rate 100 Hz, latency < 30 ms.
· Vibrotactile array (stride/wingbeat rhythm): A 4×2 array on the lower back delivers rhythmic pulses synchronised with the exoskeleton’s stride and wingbeat frequency. Update rate 100 Hz.
· Bone‑conduction audio (speed / efficiency): A bone‑conduction headset provides continuous pitch‑coded feedback: forward speed mapped to tone frequency, lift‑to‑drag efficiency mapped to timbre. Latency < 50 ms.
· Augmented reality (horizon / ZMP): AR glasses (e.g., Microsoft HoloLens 2) overlay an artificial horizon, a ZMP reticle, and a coloured “efficiency ring.” Latency < 20 ms for critical symbology.

These feedback loops are independent of the BCI and are processed by the copilot’s real‑time subsystem, ensuring they remain active even if the BCI fails.

