7.3 Phase 3 – Outdoor Combined Running‑Flight Trials (Year 3)

Objective. Demonstrate the full augmented‑body system in an outdoor environment, measuring top speed, sustained lift, and metabolic cost.

Setup.

· Full‑scale leg‑wing exoskeleton (total mass 18 kg, power 3 kW from a compact turbine generator).
· GPS + IMU ground truth.
· Safety: a lightweight parachute automatically deployed if the copilot detects an unrecoverable state.

Metrics.

· Peak speed (m/s) and sustained flight duration (s).
· Metabolic cost (VO₂) compared with unassisted running.
· Number of CBF interventions per minute.
· Subjective NASA‑TLX workload.

Statistical test.
Comparison of top speed and flight duration between full‑autonomy, shared‑autonomy (4‑DOF BCI), and direct full‑DOF BCI (attempted). The prediction is that shared autonomy will achieve >80% of full‑autonomy performance, while direct control will be unstable and terminated early by the safety copilot.

