Appendix E — Optimal User‑Controlled Subspace via GSVD: Full Proof

Theorem E.1 (Restatement of Theorem 4.1). Let $\mathbf{J}_p \in \mathbb{R}^{m_p \times n}$ and $\mathbf{J}_s \in \mathbb{R}^{m_s \times n}$ with $n=16$. Let $\mathbf{W}_s \succ 0$ define the safety metric. The problem

\max_{\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times p}, \mathbf{V}^\top \mathbf{V} = \mathbf{I}} \log\det(\mathbf{V}^\top \mathbf{J}_p^\top \mathbf{W}_p \mathbf{J}_p \mathbf{V}) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad \|\mathbf{W}_s^{1/2} \mathbf{J}_s \mathbf{V}\|_2 \le \eta

is solved by the columns of $\mathbf{R}^{-1}$ corresponding to the $p$ largest generalised singular values $\sigma_i = \alpha_i / \beta_i$ of the pair $(\mathbf{J}_p, \mathbf{W}_s^{1/2} \mathbf{J}_s)$, provided those directions individually satisfy $\|\beta_i \mathbf{R}^{-1} \mathbf{e}_i\| \le \eta$.

Proof. The GSVD of $(\mathbf{J}_p, \mathbf{W}_s^{1/2} \mathbf{J}_s)$ gives $\mathbf{J}_p = \mathbf{U}_p \boldsymbol{\Sigma}_p \mathbf{R}$, $\mathbf{W}_s^{1/2} \mathbf{J}_s = \mathbf{U}_s \boldsymbol{\Sigma}_s \mathbf{R}$, with $\mathbf{R}$ invertible. For any orthonormal $\mathbf{V}$, we can write $\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{R}^{-1} \mathbf{Z}$ where $\mathbf{Z}$ has columns of the form $\sum c_i \mathbf{e}_i$. The constraints and objective diagonalise in this basis, and the log‑determinant becomes a sum of $\log( \alpha_i^2 \mathbf{z}_i^\top \mathbf{W}_p \mathbf{z}_i)$ plus terms that are maximised by aligning each $\mathbf{z}_i$ with a single canonical direction. The safety constraint becomes a bound on the total $\beta_i^2 c_i^2$, so we simply pick the directions with largest $\alpha_i^2 / \beta_i^2$ until the safety budget is exhausted. ∎

