Appendix G — Stability of the Blending Law

The blending factor $\rho(t)$ varies slowly. We prove that the closed‑loop system is ISS with respect to $\dot{\rho}$.

G.1 Augmented Error Dynamics. Treat the blended reference $\mathbf{u}_{\text{ref}}(t) = \rho(t) \mathbf{u}_{\text{hum}}(t) + (1-\rho(t))\mathbf{u}_{\text{auto}}(t)$ as a time‑varying input. The error dynamics (5.1) become a non‑autonomous system. Because $\dot{\rho}$ is bounded by $1/\tau_\rho \approx 3.3$ s⁻¹, and the human and autonomous commands are bounded, the derivative of the reference is bounded. Applying the same Lyapunov–Krasovskii functional, the additional term from the time variation of the reference is linear in $\dot{\rho}$ and can be absorbed into the disturbance $\mathbf{w}$ without changing the ISS gain. Therefore, the blending does not destabilise.

