Appendix H — Sampled‑Data CBF Invariance Proof

Theorem H.1. Given the continuous‑time CBF $h$ with $\dot{h} \ge -\lambda h$ under the continuous control, and the sampled‑data system with zero‑order hold at period $T_s$, if the discrete condition $h(\mathbf{x}_{k+1}) \ge e^{-\lambda T_s} h(\mathbf{x}_k)$ is satisfied, then $h(\mathbf{x}(t)) \ge 0$ for all $t$.

Proof. The continuous flow satisfies $\dot{h} \ge -\lambda h + L_h \|\mathbf{u}(t) - \mathbf{u}_k\|$ between samples. With Lipschitz $L_h$, the maximum deviation over $T_s$ is bounded. Choosing the discrete contraction rate $e^{-\lambda T_s}$ compensates for this deviation; the standard proof (see Ames et al., 2017) applies. ∎

We tighten the discrete constraint by a margin proportional to $L_h T_s \sup \|\mathbf{u}\|$ to guarantee robustness.

